KG42.register("rules-b9405b2f5701110794b4ab80",{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R016","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R016","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-ancillary-service","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The allocated service quantity is used to calculate the customer's reward from the utility: Equation (23) multiplies the procured quantity by the ancillary-service price. Scope: Forward ancillary-service procurement among customers in the P2P community, for each target-period time slot. Condition: A Type-1 ancillary-service quantity is procured from a customer through the community procurement-allocation procedure. Prices specified in the affected P2P agreements enter the monetary adjustments. Compensation uses each agreement's price minus the feed-in tariff, multiplied by its reduced demand component and time-slot duration; the electricity payment avoided for that component uses the agreement's full price. Scope: Monetary adjustments to existing P2P energy trading agreements for Type-1 ancillary-service provision. Condition: The customer's baseline net load is positive, and Type-1 service reduces demand originally supplied through P2P agreements. The additional generated electricity is purchased by the utility at the feed-in tariff rate. Scope: Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. Condition: More electricity is generated in the ancillary-service adjustment. The additional consumed electricity is supplied by the utility at its retail price. Scope: Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. Condition: More electricity is consumed in the ancillary-service adjustment. An extra payment is owed to compensate the relevant customers for their revenue loss. Scope: Table 1 compensation arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. Condition: The ancillary-service adjustment violates a P2P energy trading agreement. No penalty is payable for the P2G agreement violation in these adjustment cases. Scope: Table 1 penalty arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. Condition: The ancillary-service adjustment violates a P2G residual-balancing agreement. The customer owes no P2G breach penalty and no longer owes the electricity charge for the demand that has been reduced. Scope: Type-1 ancillary-service demand reduction originally supplied under P2G residual-balancing agreements. Condition: The customer's baseline net load is positive, and the reduced demand was originally supplied by the utility.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R016-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R016-E002","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R016-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Forward ancillary-service procurement among customers in the P2P community, for each target-period time slot. | Monetary adjustments to existing P2P energy trading agreements for Type-1 ancillary-service provision. | Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. | Table 1 compensation arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. | Table 1 penalty arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. | Type-1 ancillary-service demand reduction originally supplied under P2G residual-balancing agreements.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R016-x-q-it","symbol":"q_{i,t}","meaning":"Magnitude of Type-1 ancillary service procured from customer i in time slot t, as decided by the quota procedure and used in the ancillary-service reward payment.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real (kW magnitude; Fig. 3 initializes the quota at 0 and allocates the service quantity)","unit":"kW","indices":["i∈I*","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","v141-b-g02-E12-fig3-quota-algorithm"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-it","symbol":"q'^{-I}_{i,t}","meaning":"Total demand-reduction component originally supplied through P2P energy trading agreements and displaced by Type-1 ancillary service for customer i in time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued component of the Type-1 demand-reduction magnitude (kW); source defines it as the part originally supplied through P2P agreements","unit":"kW","indices":["i∈I*","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21-eq31-p2p-award-allocation","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-itg","symbol":"q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}","meaning":"Component of the P2P-supplied demand reduction q'^{-I}_{i,t} attributed to P2P energy trading agreement g for customer i in time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued component of the P2P-supplied demand reduction (kW); source sums these components over contributing agreements g","unit":"kW","indices":["i∈I*","t∈T","g∼AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21-eq31-p2p-award-allocation","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qdoubleprime-II-it","symbol":"q''^{-II}_{i,t}","meaning":"Demand-reduction component originally supplied by the utility through P2G residual balancing and displaced by Type-1 ancillary service.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued component of the Type-1 demand-reduction magnitude (kW); source identifies it as the part originally supplied by the utility through P2G residual balancing","unit":"kW","indices":["i∈I*","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19-eq29-demand-reduction-parts","v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qdouble-it","symbol":"q''_{i,t}","meaning":"Generation-increase component of Type-1 ancillary service that drives a positive baseline net load below zero.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real (kW); defined as 0 when q_{i,t} ≤ NL*_{i,t} and as q_{i,t} − NL*_{i,t} otherwise","unit":"kW","indices":["i∈I*","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17-eq25-27-decomposition","v141-b-g02-E18-eq28-additional-generation-benefit"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pAS-t","symbol":"p_t^{AS}","meaning":"Ancillary-service price published by the utility for time slot t, used in the Type-1 ancillary-service reward formula.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"£/kW/h","indices":["t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pFiT-t","symbol":"p_t^{FiT}","meaning":"Feed-in tariff rate for time slot t at which the utility purchases additional exported or generated electricity.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"£/kWh","indices":["t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16-eq24-export-benefit","v141-b-g02-E18-eq28-additional-generation-benefit","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pretail-t","symbol":"p_t^{retail}","meaning":"Electricity retail price at which the utility supplies additional consumed electricity, and against which avoided retail cost is valued.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"£/kWh","indices":["t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pi-gt","symbol":"\\pi_{g,t}","meaning":"Price specified in the P2P energy trading agreement g for time slot t, used in the monetary adjustment for displaced P2P-supplied demand.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"£/kWh","indices":["g","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-Delta-t","symbol":"\\Delta t","meaning":"Duration of a time slot.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"hour","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16-eq24-export-benefit","v141-b-g02-E18-eq28-additional-generation-benefit","v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-NLstar-it","symbol":"NL^*_{i,t}","meaning":"Baseline net load of customer i in time slot t before ancillary-service provision, calculated in Section 3.2; positive values denote imports and negative values denote exports.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["i∈I*","t∈T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The allocated service quantity is used to calculate the customer's reward from the utility: Equation (23) multiplies the procured quantity by the ancillary-service price. Scope: Forward ancillary-service procurement among customers in the P2P community, for each target-period time slot. Condition: A Type-1 ancillary-service quantity is procured from a customer through the community procurement-allocation procedure.","expression":"\\Delta B^{AS}_{q_{i,t}} = p_t^{AS}\\cdot q_{i,t}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R016-x-q-it"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-theta-pAS-t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Prices specified in the affected P2P agreements enter the monetary adjustments. Compensation uses each agreement's price minus the feed-in tariff, multiplied by its reduced demand component and time-slot duration; the electricity payment avoided for that component uses the agreement's full price. Scope: Monetary adjustments to existing P2P energy trading agreements for Type-1 ancillary-service provision. Condition: The customer's baseline net load is positive, and Type-1 service reduces demand originally supplied through P2P agreements.","expression":"\\Delta C^{PEN}_{q'^{-I}_{i,t}} = \\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}(\\pi_{g,t}-p_t^{FiT})\\cdot q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0; \\quad \\Delta B^{RED}_{q'^{-I}_{i,t}} = \\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}\\pi_{g,t}\\cdot q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-it","v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-itg"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-theta-pi-gt","v141-c-R016-theta-pFiT-t","v141-c-R016-theta-Delta-t","v141-c-R016-theta-NLstar-it"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The additional generated electricity is purchased by the utility at the feed-in tariff rate. Scope: Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. Condition: More electricity is generated in the ancillary-service adjustment.","expression":"\\Delta B^{EXP}_{q_{i,t}} = p_t^{FiT}\\cdot q_{i,t}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}\\le 0; \\quad \\Delta B^{EXP}_{q''_{i,t}} = p_t^{FiT}\\cdot q''_{i,t}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R016-x-q-it","v141-c-R016-x-qdouble-it"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-theta-pFiT-t","v141-c-R016-theta-Delta-t","v141-c-R016-theta-NLstar-it"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","v141-b-g02-E16-eq24-export-benefit","v141-b-g02-E18-eq28-additional-generation-benefit"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The additional consumed electricity is supplied by the utility at its retail price. Scope: Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. Condition: More electricity is consumed in the ancillary-service adjustment.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"An extra payment is owed to compensate the relevant customers for their revenue loss. Scope: Table 1 compensation arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. Condition: The ancillary-service adjustment violates a P2P energy trading agreement.","expression":"\\Delta C^{PEN}_{q'^{-I}_{i,t}} = \\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}(\\pi_{g,t}-p_t^{FiT})\\cdot q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-it","v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-itg"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-theta-pi-gt","v141-c-R016-theta-pFiT-t","v141-c-R016-theta-Delta-t","v141-c-R016-theta-NLstar-it"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"No penalty is payable for the P2G agreement violation in these adjustment cases. Scope: Table 1 penalty arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. Condition: The ancillary-service adjustment violates a P2G residual-balancing agreement.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The customer owes no P2G breach penalty and no longer owes the electricity charge for the demand that has been reduced. Scope: Type-1 ancillary-service demand reduction originally supplied under P2G residual-balancing agreements. Condition: The customer's baseline net load is positive, and the reduced demand was originally supplied by the utility.","expression":"\\Delta B^{RED}_{q''^{-II}_{i,t}} = p_t^{retail}\\cdot q''^{-II}_{i,t}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R016-x-qdoubleprime-II-it"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-theta-pretail-t","v141-c-R016-theta-Delta-t","v141-c-R016-theta-NLstar-it"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 278 (2020) 115671 ng After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy trading community (a time window can be defined in the Agreement Period for this purpose), the power utility needs to decide which of and to what extent the bids are to be accepted/declined. To achieve the fairness, the power utility in principle should distribute the amount of services to be procured averagely on the customers who have submitted the bids. However, the amount of services to be procured from each customer (called as the 'quota') calculated in this way may be higher than some customers' bids, and thus the surplus quotas can be given to other customers in need. With the above considerations, the process detailed in Fig. 3 is proposed for the power utility to decide the amount of services to be procured from the customers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M03-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"kW, then q i,t = 5 kW and q i,t = 3 kW, and the net load of the customer i after service provision w","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The arrangements for addressing the conflicts among P2P energy trading, P2G residual balancing and ancillary service agreements.\nThe change in electricity production/consumption for providing ancillary services | How the change is balanced | Agreements violated | Penalty\nMore electricity generated | Purchased by the power utility at the Feed-in Tariff rate | P2P | Yes (Extra payment for compensating the revenue loss of relevant customers)\nMore electricity generated | Purchased by the power utility at the Feed-in Tariff rate | P2G | No\nMore electricity consumed | Supplied by the power utility at its retail price | P2P | Yes (Extra payment for compensating the revenue loss of relevant customers)\nMore electricity consumed | Supplied by the power utility at its retail price | P2G | No"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Without loss of generality, it is assumed that the magnitude of Type-1 AS procured from a customer i","equation_id":"(23)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Without loss of generality, it is assumed that the magnitude of Type-1 AS procured from a customer i for the time slot t is \\(q_{i,t}\\) (kW), as decided through the procedure shown in Fig. 3. Recall that the Type-1 AS refers to the demand reduction or generation increase of the customer i as a whole, which is measured with the baseline being the net load profile of the customer, \\(NL^*_{i,t}\\), calculated in Section 3.2. First of all, because of the provision of the ancillary service, the customer will receive reward from the power utility, as presented in Section 5.1.2. The associated benefit, \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{AS}\\), is expressed as \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{AS}=p_t^{AS}\\cdot q_{i,t}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T.\\) (23)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"qi,t t i,t i,t -1 For the demand reduction component q’i,t, it can be further divided ed into two pa","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For the reduction of the demand which is originally supplied by the power utility, i.e. for \\(q''^{-II}_{i,t}\\), no penalty cost needs to be paid by the customer for the breach of the P2G residual balancing agreements, according to Section 5.1.3. Furthermore, the customer will no longer need to pay the electricity cost for the demand that has been reduced. This can be seen as a 'benefit' and is calculated by \\(\\Delta B_{q''^{-II}_{i,t}}^{RED}=p_t^{retail}\\cdot q''^{-II}_{i,t}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.\\) (30)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"qi,t , , For the reduction of the demand which is originally supplied by the other customers through","equation_id":"(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to Section 5.1.3, the level of penalty cost equals to the revenue loss of the relevant customers who have to directly trade with the power utility instead because of the demand reduction. Therefore, the penalty cost that needs to be paid by the customer i in this regard is expressed as \\(\\Delta C_{q'^{-I}_{i,t}}^{PEN}=\\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}(\\pi_{g,t}-p_t^{FiT})\\cdot q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.\\) (32) Recall that \\(\\pi_g\\) is the price specified in the P2P energy trading agreement."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. no longer need to pay the relevant electricity cost specified in the rele­ sl vant P2","equation_id":"(33)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"On the other hand, the reduction of \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}\\) makes the customer no longer need to pay the relevant electricity cost specified in the relevant P2P energy trading agreements. This can be seen as a sort of benefit, and is expressed as \\(\\Delta B_{q'^{-I}_{i,t}}^{RED}=\\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}\\pi_{g,t}\\cdot q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.\\) (33)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"of the net load of a customer as a whole, rather than the change of power output/consumption of spec","equation_id":"(15)-(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As the first step, based on the assessment of the future operational status of power systems, the power utility will broadcast the total demand and prices of ancillary services to all the customers in the P2P energy trading community: \\(D^{AS}=\\{D_t^{AS}\\,|\\,t\\in T\\}\\), (15) \\(p^{AS}=\\{p_t^{AS}\\,|\\,t\\in T\\}\\), (16) where \\(D^{AS}\\) is the set of the magnitude (kW) of the ancillary services required for the time slots within the Target Time Period T, and \\(p^{AS}\\) is the set of prices (£/kW/h) that the power utility is willing to pay for the ancillary services provided by the customers. The power utility will also specify the type of ancillary services needed (either 'Type-1 AS' or 'Type-2 AS'). Note that how the power utility decides \\(D^{AS}\\) and \\(p^{AS}\\) involves comprehensive analysis of the power systems managed by the power utility, which is out of the scope of this paper."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E12-fig3-quota-algorithm","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c2r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"7) he at he d. he e­ Fig. 3. Distribution of the ancillary service procurement among customers. 6","equation_id":"(18)-(22)","figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Distribution of the ancillary service procurement among customers (for each time slot t in the Target Time Period T)\nInitialization:\nInitialize the amount of ancillary service to be procured from each customer (i.e. the 'quota'), \\(q_{i,t}\\), by \\(q_{i,t}=0\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*\\), (18) and initialize the sum of the surplus quotas of all customers, \\(Q_t=D_t^{AS}\\). (19)\nStep I:\nFirst generate the set of customers whose quotas are lower than their bids by \\(I^{**}=\\{i\\in I^*\\,|\\,q_{i,t}-b_{i,t}^{AS}\u003c0\\}\\). (20)\nThen distribute the total surplus quota averagely on the customers who need more quotas by \\(q_{i,t}=q_{i,t}+\\frac{Q_t}{|I^{**}|}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^{**}\\). (21)\nStep II:\nCalculate the total surplus quota by \\(Q_t=\\sum_{i\\in I^*}(\\max(q_{i,t}-b_{i,t}^{AS},0))\\). (22)\nIf \\(Q_t\\ne 0\\) and \\(I^{**}\\ne \\varnothing\\), go back to Step I. Otherwise, continue to Step III.\nStep III:\nDecide the amount of ancillary service to be procured from each customer according to the following logic (presented as pseudo-codes):\n1. if \\(q_{i,t}\\ge b_{i,t}^{AS}\\)\n2. \\(q_{i,t}=b_{i,t}^{AS}\\)\n3. else\n4. the customer i chooses a value from \\([0,q_{i,t}]\\) as the final \\(q_{i,t}\\)\n5. end if"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E16-eq24-export-benefit","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Without loss of generality, it is assumed that the magnitude of Type-1 AS procured from a customer i","equation_id":"(24)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"If \\(NL^*_{i,t}\\le 0\\), to provide Type-1 AS, the customer needs to export more electricity, as much as \\(q_{i,t}\\). As specified in Section 5.1.3, the power utility will purchase all the \\(q_{i,t}\\) at the Feed-in Tariff rate. Therefore, the customer will receive extra benefit, \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{EXP}\\) (£), as calculated by \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{EXP}=p_t^{FiT}\\cdot q_{i,t}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}\\le 0.\\) (24)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17-eq25-27-decomposition","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"qi,t , , If NL*i,t > 0, qi,t can be divided into two parts, i.e. ot qi,t = q’i,t + q’’i,t ∀i ∈I*, t ","equation_id":"(25)-(27)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"If \\(NL^*_{i,t}>0\\), \\(q_{i,t}\\) can be divided into two parts, i.e. \\(q_{i,t}=q'_{i,t}+q''_{i,t}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0,\\) (25) where \\(q'_{i,t}=q_{i,t}\\) if \\(q_{i,t}\\le NL^*_{i,t}\\), and \\(q'_{i,t}=NL^*_{i,t}\\) if \\(q_{i,t}>NL^*_{i,t}\\). (26) \\(q''_{i,t}=0\\) if \\(q_{i,t}\\le NL^*_{i,t}\\), and \\(q''_{i,t}=q_{i,t}-NL^*_{i,t}\\) if \\(q_{i,t}>NL^*_{i,t}\\). (27) In Equations (25)-(27), \\(q'_{i,t}\\) (kW) represents the 'demand reduction component' that decreases the \\(NL^*_{i,t}\\) towards 0, while \\(q''_{i,t}\\) (kW) represents the 'generation increase component' that drives the \\(NL^*_{i,t}\\) towards a more negative value (i.e. changing the customer i from a consumer to a producer)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18-eq28-additional-generation-benefit","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 278 (2020) 115671 For another example, if it is assumed that NL*i,t = 5 kW and qi,t =","equation_id":"(28)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For the additional electricity generation of the customer, i.e. \\(q''_{i,t}\\), because of the provision of Type-1 AS, the power utility will purchase it at the Feed-in Tariff rate according to Section 5.1.3. Therefore, the additional benefit because of this, \\(\\Delta B_{q''_{i,t}}^{EXP}\\) (£), is calculated by \\(\\Delta B_{q''_{i,t}}^{EXP}=p_t^{FiT}\\cdot q''_{i,t}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.\\) (28)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19-eq29-demand-reduction-parts","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"qi,t t i,t i,t -1 For the demand reduction component q’i,t, it can be further divided ed into two pa","equation_id":"(29)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For the demand reduction component \\(q'_{i,t}\\), it can be further divided into two parts: \\(q'_{i,t}=q'^{-I}_{i,t}+q''^{-II}_{i,t}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0,\\) (29) where \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}\\) (kW) represents the component that is originally supplied by other customers through P2P energy trading agreements (denoted as \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}\\)), and \\(q''^{-II}_{i,t}\\) (kW) represents the component that is originally supplied by the power utility through P2G residual balancing agreements (denoted as \\(q''^{-II}_{i,t}\\sim AGRT^{P2G}_{i,t}\\))."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E21-eq31-p2p-award-allocation","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"qi,t , , For the reduction of the demand which is originally supplied by the other customers through","equation_id":"(31)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For the reduction of the demand which is originally supplied by the other customers through P2P energy trading agreements, i.e. for \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}\\), the customers need to pay penalty cost to those customers. The \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}\\) may be originally supplied by multiple P2P energy trading agreements, which is expressed by \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}=\\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0,\\) (31) where g represents a P2P energy trading agreement that contributes to \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}\\)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-bidding","v141-a-M03-clearing","v141-a-M03-coordination","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","quote":"To achieve the fairness, the power utility in principle should distribute the amount of services to be procured averagely on the customers who have submitted the bids."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","quote":"Without loss of generality, it is assumed that the magnitude of Type-1 AS procured from a customer i for the time slot t is \\(q_{i,t}\\) (kW), as decided through the procedure shown in Fig. 3."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","quote":"First of all, because of the provision of the ancillary service, the customer will receive reward from the power utility, as presented in Section 5.1.2. The associated benefit, \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{AS}\\), is expressed as \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{AS}=p_t^{AS}\\cdot q_{i,t}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T.\\) (23)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","quote":"Therefore, the penalty cost that needs to be paid by the customer i in this regard is expressed as \\(\\Delta C_{q'^{-I}_{i,t}}^{PEN}=\\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}(\\pi_{g,t}-p_t^{FiT})\\cdot q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.\\) (32) Recall that \\(\\pi_g\\) is the price specified in the P2P energy trading agreement."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit","quote":"On the other hand, the reduction of \\(q'^{-I}_{i,t}\\) makes the customer no longer need to pay the relevant electricity cost specified in the relevant P2P energy trading agreements. This can be seen as a sort of benefit, and is expressed as \\(\\Delta B_{q'^{-I}_{i,t}}^{RED}=\\sum_{g\\sim AGRT^{P2P}_{i,t}}\\pi_{g,t}\\cdot q'^{-I}_{i,t,g}\\cdot\\Delta t\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T\\quad \\text{when } NL^*_{i,t}>0.\\) (33)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","quote":"More electricity generated | Purchased by the power utility at the Feed-in Tariff rate"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","quote":"More electricity consumed | Supplied by the power utility at its retail price"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","quote":"More electricity generated | Purchased by the power utility at the Feed-in Tariff rate | P2P | Yes (Extra payment for compensating the revenue loss of relevant customers)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","quote":"More electricity consumed | Supplied by the power utility at its retail price | P2P | Yes (Extra payment for compensating the revenue loss of relevant customers)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","quote":"More electricity generated | Purchased by the power utility at the Feed-in Tariff rate | P2G | No"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","quote":"More electricity consumed | Supplied by the power utility at its retail price | P2G | No"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit","quote":"For the reduction of the demand which is originally supplied by the power utility, i.e. for \\(q''^{-II}_{i,t}\\), no penalty cost needs to be paid by the customer for the breach of the P2G residual balancing agreements, according to Section 5.1.3. Furthermore, the customer will no longer need to pay the electricity cost for the demand that has been reduced."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"2298e93fe291592c10dd71796334b557b102966c09f999095566c6f59d2b251d","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Partially formalized from the supplied, still-unreviewed B evidence: C001 uses Eq. (23), C002 uses Eqs. (32)-(33), C003 uses Eqs. (24) and (28), C005 uses Eq. (32), and C007 uses Eq. (30). C004 and C006 remain not_formalized because Table 1 provides only qualitative payment instructions and the source explicitly omits Type-2 equations; no C.1 graph change is requested.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-x-q-it","node_ids":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R016-E001"],"rationale":"The procured Type-1 AS quantity is the clearing-local quota that Equation (23) uses as the multiplier in the settlement.payment reward."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-it","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The P2P-supplied demand-reduction component is a settlement-payment quantity used in the monetary adjustment formulas (32)-(33)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qprime-I-itg","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The per-agreement decomposed P2P-supplied demand reduction enters the settlement.payment penalty and avoided-cost formulas."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qdoubleprime-II-it","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The utility-supplied demand-reduction component enters the settlement.payment avoided-retail-cost formula (30)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-x-qdouble-it","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The generation-increase component enters the settlement.payment feed-in-tariff benefit formula (28)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pAS-t","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The utility-set ancillary-service price is a parameter of the settlement.payment reward formula; its publication stage is outside this rule's frozen V."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pFiT-t","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The feed-in tariff is a settlement-payment parameter for additional generation and for the P2P penalty benchmark."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pretail-t","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The retail electricity price is a settlement-payment parameter for avoided utility-supplied demand cost."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-pi-gt","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R016-E002"],"rationale":"The P2P agreement price is represented through pricing.local and enters the monetary adjustment at settlement.payment via the frozen pricing-to-settlement edge."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-Delta-t","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Time-slot duration is a settlement-payment conversion parameter in the energy-price formulas."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-theta-NLstar-it","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The baseline net load is a settlement condition parameter selecting the positive or non-positive payment branch."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R016-E001"],"rationale":"C001 formalizes the clearing-local procured quantity being paid at the utility ancillary-service price in settlement.payment, exactly along frozen edge E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C002","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R016-E002"],"rationale":"C002 formalizes P2P agreement prices entering monetary adjustments at settlement.payment along the frozen pricing-to-settlement edge E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 is a settlement.payment rule for additional generated electricity; its supported formulas are Eqs. (24) and (28)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C004","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C004 is a settlement.payment rule, but the source gives only a qualitative Table 1 instruction and no equation for the additional-consumption branch."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C005","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C005 formalizes the supported Type-1 P2P-displacement extra-payment branch as a settlement.payment penalty cost; the Type-2 branch has no explicit source equation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C006","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C006 is a settlement.payment no-penalty rule, but the source gives only Table 1 prose and no explicit P2G zero-penalty equation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C007","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C007 formalizes the supported avoided-retail-cost benefit in Eq. (30) at settlement.payment; the no-penalty clause remains prose."}],"revision_requests":["No C.1 graph revision is requested: the frozen nodes and edges can host the supported payment formulas.","B re-extraction remains desirable for Type-2 AS: the source states that the Type-2 cost and benefit analysis is not presented in detail, so C004 and the Type-2 branch of C005/C006 cannot be written as equations.","B re-extraction remains desirable for an explicit P2G no-penalty equation: the source gives only prose for the zero P2G penalty in C006 and for the no-penalty part of C007."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
